{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>All these are the tribes of Israel.</b> Those that Jacob mentioned here are truly the twelve tribes, which were written upon the breastplate and the ephod as a remembrance before HaShem, and which stood in the covenant of Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal. Corresponding to them Moses set up twelve monuments, Joshua set up stones in the Jordan and at Gilgal, and Elijah set up stones on the altar. But Manasseh and Ephraim were not counted among the tribes, except in the matter of inheriting the land and what follows from it, due to the absence of the tribe of Levi." "<b>And he blessed them.</b> In addition to what he said above." "<b>Every one according to his blessing he blessed them.</b> To each one he gave a blessing uniquely needed by him — for example, to Judah in the matter of kingship, to Issachar in the matter of Torah, and to Levi in the matter of the divine service."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:30.358234234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}